<main className={"view"}> <nav className={"secbar"} aria-label={"Physician writing"}> <div className={"wrap secbar__in"}> <p className={"secbar__k"}><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a></p> <ul className={"secbar__l"}> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-564"}>{"Papers "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> <li className={"has-sub"}><button className={"sbtrig"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"sbd-565"}>{"Support "}<svg className={"chev"} viewBox={"0 0 12 12"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M2 4l4 4 4-4"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.7"} /></svg></button></li> </ul> <a className={"secbar__cta"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Send the case "}<svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"} /></svg></a> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-564"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"}>{"Case report"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/original-research-article/"}>{"Original research article"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-manuscripts/"}>{"Physician manuscripts"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/clinical-literature-review-for-an-evidence-based-medicine/"}>{"Clinical literature review"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"sbdrop"} id={"sbd-565"} hidden={true}> <div className={"sbdrop__l"}> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/research-proposal/"}>{"Research proposal"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/literature-search-and-citation/"}>{"Literature search & citation"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/customized-writing/"}>{"Customized writing"}</a> <a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/physician-training/"}>{"Physician training"}</a> </div> </div> </nav> <div className={"crumbar"}> <div className={"wrap"}> <p><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M3 10.2 12 3l9 7.2V20a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5v-6H9v6H4a1 1 0 0 1-1-1z"} /></svg><a href={"/"} data-nav={""}>{"Home"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/"}>{"Services"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><a href={"/services/physician-writing-services/"}>{"Physician writing"}</a><i>{"›"}</i><em>{"Physician Manuscript Writing Service"}</em></p> <span className={"crumbar__tag"}>{"Research that survives peer review"}</span> </div> </div> <section className={"phero"}> <div className={"wrap phero__in"}> <div> <h1>{"Physician Manuscript Writing Service"}</h1> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"Most clinicians who want to publish are not short of material. They are short of uninterrupted hours, and short of one specific piece of knowledge: which kind of paper the thing they have actually makes. Ten patients written up as a case series waste the denominator that would have made them a cohort study; a trial written to the wrong reporting guideline has to be restructured rather than edited. Pubrica’s physician manuscript writing service starts by settling that question, then writes the paper to the guideline the design requires — original research articles, case series, audits, reviews, short reports, commentaries and letters — formatted to your target journal, with the authorship and disclosure handled the way the ICMJE expects."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions"}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#pm-router"}>{"Find out what your data makes"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"#fsm-pm"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pm"}>{"See a sample"}</a> </div> </div> <figure className={"jmatch rv is-in"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <figcaption className={"jmatch__bar"}> <span><b>{"One decision at a glance"}</b>{" · 14 charts on a shelf"}</span> <span>{"Series, or cohort?"}</span> </figcaption> <div className={"jmatch__body"}> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Written as a case series"}</b><span>{"No denominator"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--no"} style={{ '--w': "32%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Written as a retrospective cohort"}</b><span>{"Rate, with a CI"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Reporting guideline it then falls under"}</b><span>{"STROBE"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "100%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Journals that will consider it"}</b><span>{"Considerably more"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--ok"} style={{ '--w': "88%" }} /></div> </div> <div className={"jm__row"}> <p className={"jm__top"}><b>{"Extra work to write it the better way"}</b><span>{"About a week"}</span></p> <div className={"jm__track"}><div className={"jm__fill jm__fill--mid"} style={{ '--w': "24%" }} /></div> </div> </div> <div className={"jmatch__foot"}> <p className={"funnel"}><b>{"Data"}</b> <i>{"→"}</i>{" article type "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" guideline "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" draft "}<i>{"→"}</i>{" journal "}<i>{"→"}</i> <b>{"decision"}</b></p> </div> </figure> </div> </section> <div className={"creds"}> <div className={"wrap creds__in"}> <span className={"creds__lab"}>{"Every manuscript"}</span> <ul className={"creds__list"}> <li>{"Article type settled first"}</li> <li>{"Written to its guideline"}</li> <li>{"Authorship agreed in writing"}</li> <li>{"Assistance declared"}</li> <li>{"Formatted to the journal"}</li> </ul> </div> </div> <div className={"proof"}><div className={"wrap proof__in"}> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"From $320"}</b><span>{"A manuscript to its reporting guideline, in 7–10 business days"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"Since 2009"}</b><span>{"Supporting clinicians through publication"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ICMJE · EQUATOR"}</b><span>{"CONSORT 2025, STROBE, STARD, PRISMA 2020, CARE, SCARE 2023"}</span></div> <div className={"proof__i"}><b>{"ISO 9001:2015"}</b><span>{"Quality management certified · cert. H3CR9TCU20251212INDQM10N"}</span></div> </div></div> <nav className={"pagenav is-scroll"} aria-label={"On this page"}><div className={"wrap pagenav__in"}><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-what-we-do-svnndw"} aria-current={"true"}>{"What we do"}</a><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-who-we-serve-1se6ds2"}>{"Who we serve"}</a><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-our-compliance-vy262n"}>{"Our compliance"}</a><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-how-it-works-158nh1c"}>{"How it works"}</a><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-our-experts-1x3gnad"}>{"Our experts"}</a><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-sample-work-1lmeyi9"}>{"Sample work"}</a><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-packages-e1hdf4"}>{"Packages"}</a><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-guarantee-1b76uud"}>{"Guarantee"}</a><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-client-stories-1q3pnx0"}>{"Client stories"}</a><a href={"#pn-physician-manuscripts-faq-qgx437"}>{"FAQ"}</a></div></nav><section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-what-we-do-svnndw"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What we do"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Eight pieces of work, and each can be commissioned on its own."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Manuscripts arrive at every stage, and the part that is missing is rarely the whole of it. Buying the part you need is cheaper than buying the package that contains it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--get rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Article type and journal strategy"}</b> <span>{"What the data makes, which guideline governs it, and which journals publish work of this design at this size. Sold on its own as a scoping conversation with a written summary, and credited against a writing package if you go on to commission one. This is the hour that most often changes the shape of a paper."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Full manuscript writing"}</b> <span>{"The complete paper written from your data and your protocol, in IMRaD or in the structure your journal uses, to the reporting guideline the design requires. Tables and figures built as part of the draft. The abstract written last, to the journal’s own headings rather than to generic ones."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Restructuring a draft you already have"}</b> <span>{"Most drafts we receive need structure rather than language. The methods are thin because they lost the word-limit fight to the introduction; the discussion reviews the field instead of arguing the finding; the claims are written in the grammar of an experiment for an observational design. None of that is proofreading."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Statistical analysis and interpretation"}</b> <span>{"Analysis in R, SPSS, STATA, SAS or Python, with the model matched to the design rather than to habit, assumptions checked, and the output returned with the code. Effect sizes with confidence intervals, missing data handled explicitly, and a clear line between what was pre-specified and what was exploratory."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"The claim audit"}</b> <span>{"Every sentence that makes a claim checked against what the design supports, with the rewrite supplied rather than just the objection. Causal verbs in an observational paper, a null result described as showing no difference when the interval says otherwise, a subgroup reported without its interaction test. This is the single highest-yield hour in the process."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Figures, tables and graphical abstracts"}</b> <span>{"Figures rebuilt to the journal’s specification rather than exported from the analysis software, tables designed to be read rather than dumped, legends written so each stands alone, and a graphical abstract where the journal asks for one. Clinical images de-identified in the file, not merely on screen."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Originality and AI-authorship screening"}</b> <span>{"iThenticate similarity screening with every match read and classified, and AI-content screening alongside. A raw percentage is close to meaningless in clinical writing, where staging criteria, drug names and standard method descriptions produce unavoidable overlap. What matters is which matches are boilerplate and which are somebody else’s sentences."}</span> </div> <div className={"cap"}> <b>{"Submission and response to reviewers"}</b> <span>{"Formatting, declarations, cover letter, conflict-screened reviewer suggestions and submission through the portal, then the point-by-point response when the reports arrive. Where a paper is rejected, an honest read of why, and a decision about whether to revise, redirect or stop — which is occasionally the right answer."}</span> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-who-we-serve-1se6ds2"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Who we serve"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Who commissions a manuscript."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Six kinds of author, and one recurring constraint: the clinical work does not stop while the paper is written."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"auds rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}><b>{"Practising and hospital-based clinicians"}</b><span>{"Doctors running audits, series and investigator-initiated studies alongside a full caseload — who need the writing handled without losing control of the clinical judgement in it. The bottleneck is uninterrupted hours, not ideas."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}><b>{"Surgeons and procedural specialists"}</b><span>{"Technique comparison, perioperative outcomes, innovation reports and complication analysis, written by people who know that a reviewer who operates will ask about the learning curve, the equipment and the operating time."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}><b>{"Academic physicians and faculty"}</b><span>{"Institution-based and translational work written for the indexed journals a department is measured by, where the paper also has to satisfy a promotion committee and a grant report at the same time."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}><b>{"Residents, fellows and postgraduates"}</b><span>{"Often a first submission, frequently against a training requirement with a date attached, and very often a thesis chapter that has to become an article — which is a rewrite rather than a trim, and the part that surprises people."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}><b>{"Private practitioners and diagnostic consultants"}</b><span>{"Clinicians outside an academic structure with genuinely interesting material, no departmental support and nobody to ask which journal takes this. That last question is usually the whole of the problem."}</span></div> <div className={"aud"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}><b>{"Industry-affiliated physicians and medical affairs teams"}</b><span>{"Company-sponsored work, where GPP 2022 applies alongside the ICMJE, the sponsor’s role in the writing is disclosed, and the publication plan has to survive being read by somebody looking for undisclosed influence."}</span></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"The three moments people call"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"The best one is when the data is complete and nothing has been drafted, because the article type can then be chosen properly, the guideline settled before it shapes anything, and the authorship written down before anybody is invested in a position. The second is with a draft in hand, which is where most manuscripts arrive and is entirely workable — though the work usually turns out to be structural rather than linguistic, and a paper that needs its claims rewritten is not a paper that needs proofreading. The third is after a rejection, which is a better moment than it feels: a reviewer’s report is the only direct evidence you will ever get of how this literature reads your work, and it is worth an hour with somebody who reads them regularly before deciding whether to revise, redirect or stop. What nobody can do is turn an underpowered study into a convincing one, and where that is the situation we will say so rather than write around it."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-our-compliance-vy262n"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our compliance and guideline standards"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The guidelines, with their current versions."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Writing to a superseded version is a visible error, and it is one of the commonest on medical writing websites. These are the versions current on 21 September 2026, taken from the issuing bodies and the EQUATOR Network."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"stds"}> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--consort"} role={"img"} aria-label={"CONSORT"} /></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"CONSORT 2025 and SPIRIT 2025 "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(trials, and trial protocols)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Both were revised in 2025 and published simultaneously across five journals. CONSORT 2025 runs to 30 items plus the flow diagram; SPIRIT 2025 to 34 items plus the timeline figure. They now share one website, consort-spirit.org, and the older consort-statement.org branding is superseded. Extensions exist for cluster, crossover, stepped-wedge, non-inferiority, pilot and N-of-1 designs, for patient-reported outcomes and for harms. Anything still citing a 2010 CONSORT checklist is fifteen years out of date, and links to PDFs on publishers’ legacy fileshares are the usual way that happens."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--word"} role={"img"} aria-label={"STROBE and STARD"}>{"STROBE"}<em>{"+ STARD · TRIPOD+AI"}</em></i></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"STROBE, STARD and TRIPOD+AI "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(observational, diagnostic and prediction)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"STROBE (2007) governs cohort, case-control and cross-sectional studies, with RECORD for routinely collected health data and STROBE-MR for Mendelian randomisation. STARD (2015) governs diagnostic accuracy, with a STARD-AI extension published in September 2025. Prediction models fall under TRIPOD+AI (2024), which replaces the 2015 TRIPOD checklist — though its explanation and elaboration paper is still pending, so the 2015 one remains the working reference for the detail. None of the three has been revised more recently than that, and claims to the contrary are worth checking."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--icmje"} role={"img"} aria-label={"ICMJE recommendations"} /></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"ICMJE recommendations "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(authorship, disclosure, registration, AI)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Updated January 2026, and the update matters: it added a new section on artificial intelligence, new guidance on authors’ access to data, and revisions to the sections on sponsor agreements and academic freedom, scientific misconduct, trial registration and reporting sources of support. Prospective registration remains a condition of consideration at member journals, and retrospective registration is permanently visible in the registry. Note that the browsable pages on the ICMJE site still carry older text in places; the PDF is the authoritative version."}</p> </div> <div className={"std rv"}> <span className={"std__mark"}><i className={"stdm stdm--gpp"} role={"img"} aria-label={"Good Publication Practice"} /></span> <p className={"std__name"}>{"GPP 2022 "}<span className={"std__ab"}>{"(company-sponsored research — and no longer GPP3)"}</span></p> <p className={"std__d"}>{"Good Publication Practice was updated in 2022 and published in the "}<i>{"Annals of Internal Medicine"}</i>{"; it supersedes GPP3, which dates from 2015. ISMPP stewards it. It governs the planning, development, review and publication of company-sponsored biomedical research and binds everybody involved — sponsor staff, investigators, authors, professional writers and agencies. It is relevant here only where a manuscript has industry sponsorship, and we say so rather than listing it on every page. GPP is "}<i>{"Good Publication Practice"}</i>{"; it has nothing to do with Good Pharmacy Practice, which is a different document about dispensing."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Where AI is used, and where it is not"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Authorship is a responsibility, and it stays with you."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"ICMJE authorship requires that somebody can be accountable for the whole paper. A tool cannot be accountable for anything, which is why no journal accepts one as an author and why undeclared use is treated as an integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps caps--3 rv rv-d1"} style={{ marginTop: "0" }}> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we use it for"}</b><span>{"Finding source material. Checking references against what they cite. Consistency across sections. Reformatting to the target journal."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What we do not use it for"}</b><span>{"Clinical interpretation; the discussion; any claim not verified against the data; and anything submitted under your name that you have not read and agreed in full."}</span></div> <div className={"cap"}><b>{"What goes in your declaration"}</b><span>{"The tool, the stage it was used at, and the human oversight applied — because journals, funders and the ICMJE January 2026 update all now expect it, and an undeclared tool found later is treated as a research integrity matter rather than a style preference."}</span></div> <div className={"caps__note"}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why we publish no accuracy figure of our own"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"These tools are marketed with precision and recall figures, and the honest problem is who measured them. In June 2026 a Cochrane journal retracted a validation study of one widely sold tool because every author held equity in the product, and the conflict had not been caught in review."}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"So Pubrica quotes no self-generated accuracy number, because ours would carry exactly the same conflict. What we will do is tell you which tool was used on your project, at which stage, and show you what a human changed after it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-how-it-works-158nh1c"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"How the physician manuscript service works"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Six stages, and the first one can change the paper."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Stage one exists because the question it answers — what does this data make — is the only one that cannot be fixed by rewriting."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"steps6"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "0" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage one"}</span> <h3>{"What the data makes, and who the authors are"}</h3> <p><b>{"Before anything is quoted."}</b>{" A clinician or biomedical scientist in your field reads what you have and settles the article type, the reporting guideline that follows from it, and the realistic journal band. This is also where the author list is written down and checked against the four ICMJE criteria — unpopular in week one, and the single thing that has saved our clients the most trouble."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "1" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage two"}</span> <h3>{"Title, abstract and the journal shortlist"}</h3> <p><b>{"Written early, because they constrain everything after them."}</b>{" A working title and a structured abstract to the target journal’s own headings — which are journal-specific, and using generic ones is a routine desk-rejection trigger. Three candidate journals with the reasoning for each, so the word limit and the structure you are writing to are real rather than assumed."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "2" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage three"}</span> <h3>{"The framework, signed off before any prose"}</h3> <p><b>{"Every section mapped to the checklist item it answers and the source its content comes from, with the words allocated."}</b>{" Moving a section at this stage takes a minute; moving it after drafting breaks every cross-reference and every figure call-out. The methods budget is fixed here and defended later, because the methods are what a reviewer reads first and what authors cut first."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "3" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage four"}</span> <h3>{"Drafting, with the analysis alongside"}</h3> <p><b>{"Written by a subject-matter writer, with a statistician where the analysis needs one."}</b>{" Effect sizes with confidence intervals, pre-specified analyses separated from exploratory ones, subgroups reported with their interaction tests. Tables and figures built as part of the draft rather than bolted on, and the abstract written last, from the paper, rather than first from the intention."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "4" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage five"}</span> <h3>{"Internal review, and the claim audit"}</h3> <p><b>{"Read by somebody who did not write it."}</b>{" Every claim checked against what the design can support — which is where most sound studies lose credibility, and which is fixable in the words rather than in the data. Then the reporting checklist completed honestly with page numbers, originality and AI-content screening, and the declarations assembled."}</p> </div> <div className={"step6"} style={{ '--i': "5" }}> <span className={"step6__n"}>{"Stage six"}</span> <h3>{"Submission and the reviewer response"}</h3> <p><b>{"Formatted, submitted and tracked."}</b>{" Cover letter written for the editor, declarations completed, suggested reviewers screened for conflicts, and the submission made through the portal. When the reports come back, a point-by-point response that concedes what should be conceded, answers what can be answered with evidence, and declines the rest with a reason rather than in silence."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap band band--split rv"}> <div> <h2>{"Send what you have. We will tell you what paper it makes."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"A spreadsheet and an idea, a folder of charts, a half-written draft, or a manuscript an editor has already returned — all four are normal starting points. Two business days, at no cost: the article type, the guideline, the realistic journal band, and an honest word about whether the work supports the claim you want to make."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "28px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"jcard"}> <div className={"jcard__bar"}>{"What you provide"}</div> <div className={"jcard__body"}> <div className={"jcard__grid"}> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The data"}</b><span>{"However it exists — a spreadsheet, an export, charts"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The design"}</b><span>{"What you did, in your own words, is enough"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The approvals"}</b><span>{"Ethics reference, registration number if there is one"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"Any draft"}</b><span>{"Part-written, a thesis chapter, or a rejected paper"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The authors"}</b><span>{"Who they are, and who decides the order"}</span></div> <div className={"jstat"}><b>{"The target"}</b><span>{"A named journal, or the kind you are aiming at"}</span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"}>{"If the paper has been rejected before, send the reviewer comments. They are the most valuable thing you can give us and the thing authors most often withhold, usually because reading them again is unpleasant. A resubmission that does not visibly answer them tends to collect the same criticism from a different reviewer — and reviewer pools in a specialty are smaller than authors imagine."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Manuscript types we write"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Fourteen kinds of paper, and what each one has to prove."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"The type is not a label on a folder. It decides which checklist a reviewer applies, which journals will consider the work, and what the paper is allowed to claim at the end."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"caps rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Original research article"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to prove the method could produce the finding. The guideline follows the design: CONSORT 2025 for a trial, STROBE for observational work, STARD for diagnostic accuracy. Written up in full on our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/original-research-article/"} data-nav={""}>{"original research article"}</a>{" page."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Case report"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to prove the case adds something and that consent exists. CARE, plus SCARE 2023 where surgical. Written up in full on our "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"} data-nav={""}>{"case report"}</a>{" page."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Case series"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to say how the patients were selected. A consecutive series and a series assembled from memory are different kinds of evidence, and the distinction is the first thing a reviewer asks about."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Systematic review"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to prove the search was reproducible and the protocol came first. PRISMA 2020, with PRISMA-S for the search. Registration after screening has begun is visible and costly."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Meta-analysis"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to justify combining the studies at all. Heterogeneity quantified and explained rather than reported as a number, and the model choice defended rather than defaulted."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Narrative and scoping review"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to be honest that it is not systematic. A narrative review presented with the furniture of a systematic one is the commonest reviewer complaint in this category."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Brief communication or short report"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to make one claim in fifteen hundred words. Often the right home for work that would make a thin full paper, and treated by editors as a category rather than a consolation."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Clinical audit and quality improvement"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to measure practice against a standard that already existed. SQUIRE 2.0 where it is a quality improvement report. Writing an audit as though it discovered something is the usual mistake."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Commentary and perspective"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to argue rather than summarise, and to declare every interest. Usually invited, occasionally not, and almost always shorter than the author first writes it."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Letter to the editor"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to be timely. Most journals will not consider a letter about an article published more than a few weeks or months earlier, and the window closes quietly."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Drug efficacy and safety study"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to keep the regulatory and journal registers apart. Where there is industry sponsorship, GPP 2022 applies alongside the ICMJE, and the sponsor’s role in the writing is disclosed."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Surgical technique and innovation"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to report the learning curve rather than imply it, name the equipment and grade the complications. A reviewer who operates will notice each omission."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Real-world evidence and health outcomes"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to describe the data source honestly: what is captured, what is missing, and who is not in it. RECORD applies where the data was routinely collected."}</p></div> <div className={"cap"}><p className={"caps__k"}>{"Conference abstract and poster"}</p><p className={"caps__t"}>{"Has to work standalone in three hundred words. Also has to be disclosed later, because a published abstract is prior publication for the purposes of the full paper."}</p></div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", borderTop: "0", marginTop: "0" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Why three of these have their own pages"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Case reports, original research articles and clinical literature reviews are the three physicians commission most, and each has enough specific process behind it — consent documentation, claim auditing, protocol registration — to be worth its own page rather than a paragraph. Everything else on this list is written here. If you are not sure which of the three you are in, the router above will tell you, and if it puts you on another page the work and the people are the same."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"The decision that comes before the writing"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What does your data actually make?"}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"This is the question that decides the reporting guideline, the length, the journals that will consider it and the months it will take — and it is almost always settled by habit rather than by the data. Fourteen patients get written up as a case series because the last one was; a comparison gets written as a description because nobody said otherwise. Answer six questions below and the router tells you what you have, which checklist governs it, and which of our pages handles it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tgrid"} data-tls={""} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"tk rv"} id={"pm-router"} data-tool={"mty"} data-open={"1"}> <div className={"tk__h"}> <p className={"tk__n"}>{"01"}</p> <div> <h3 className={"tk__t"}><button type={"button"} aria-expanded={"true"} aria-controls={"pm-router-body"}>{"Manuscript type router"}</button></h3> <p className={"tk__s"}>{"From what you have to what it is: the article type, the guideline that governs it, the length, the turnaround and an indicative price."}</p> <span className={"tk__tag"}>{"Runs in your browser · nothing sent anywhere"}</span> </div> <span className={"tk__x"} aria-hidden={"true"} /> </div> <div className={"tk__body"} id={"pm-router-body"}> <div className={"tfm"}> <div className={"tf tf--wide"}><span id={"lbl-pm-have"}>{"What do you have?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"have"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-pm-have"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"one"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"Patients you treated"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"trial"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"An intervention you tested"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"obs"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Data you collected or extracted"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"diag"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A test or a prediction model"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"lit"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Published studies to synthesise"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"audit"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Practice measured against a standard"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"opinion"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A view on somebody else’s work"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"abs"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"A meeting deadline"}</button></div></div> <label className={"tf"} data-when={"have:one|obs|lit"}><span>{"How many patients, records or studies?"}</span><em>{"The number is what decides whether this is a series or a study."}</em><input type={"number"} data-k={"n"} value={"1"} step={1} min={1} /></label> <div className={"tf"} data-when={"have:trial|obs|diag"} hidden={true}><span id={"lbl-pm-arm"}>{"Are you comparing groups?"}</span><div className={"tseg"} data-seg={"arm"} role={"group"} aria-labelledby={"lbl-pm-arm"}><button type={"button"} data-v={"one"} aria-pressed={"true"}>{"One group only"}</button><button type={"button"} data-v={"multi"} aria-pressed={"false"}>{"Two or more compared"}</button></div></div> <label className={"tf"}><span>{"Word limit you are writing to"}</span><em>{"Your target journal’s figure, not a general one."}</em><input type={"number"} data-k={"words"} value={"3000"} step={250} min={300} /></label> <div className={"tchk tf--wide"}> <label data-when={"have:trial"} hidden={true}><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"rand"} checked={true} /><span>{"Participants were randomly allocated"}</span></label> <label data-when={"have:obs"} hidden={true}><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"pros"} /><span>{"Data was collected prospectively, to a plan written first"}</span></label> <label><input type={"checkbox"} data-k={"stat"} checked={true} /><span>{"The analysis still needs doing, or needs checking"}</span></label> </div> </div> <div className={"tout"} data-out={""}><div className={"tout__hd"}><b>{"Case report"}</b><span>{"5 to 12 business days"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"What it is"}</b><span>{"Case report"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Reporting guideline"}</b><span>{"CARE (2013, with the 2017 explanation and elaboration paper); SCARE 2023 as well where the substance is an operation"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Typical length"}</b><span>{"1,000 to 3,000 words in the body, excluding abstract and references"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Typical turnaround"}</b><span>{"5 to 12 business days"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Indicative price"}</b><span>{"From $210, with the scope cap set at quote"}</span></div><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Statistical support"}</b><span>{"Included in the quote rather than added later. The model is matched to the design before drafting, because a paper written around the wrong analysis has to be rewritten rather than corrected."}</span></div><div className={"tverd"}><p><b>{"Why that guideline."}</b>{" Thirteen items, of which the dated timeline is the one most often missing and the patient perspective the one most often skipped."}</p><p><b>{"Your word limit."}</b> <span className={"tflag tflag--ok"}>{"Workable"}</span>{" Workable. 3,000 words sits within the normal range for this type."}</p></div><p className={"tsub"}>{"Where this is handled"}</p><div className={"trow trow--txt"}><b>{"Case report writing"}</b><span><a className={"tlink"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"} data-nav={""}>{"Open that page"}</a>{" for the process, the packages and the sample work for this article type."}</span></div><p className={"tmeth"}><b>{"How this was worked out."}</b>{" The article type follows from what the data is rather than from what it is called: a series of ten or more patients with a denominator is an observational study whatever the author has been calling it, and writing it as a series wastes the denominator. Guidelines and versions are as published by the issuing bodies and listed by the EQUATOR Network: CARE 2013 with the 2017 explanation and elaboration paper, SCARE 2023 and PROCESS 2023 in the "}<i>{"International Journal of Surgery"}</i>{", CONSORT 2025 and SPIRIT 2025 at consort-spirit.org, STROBE 2007, STARD 2015, TRIPOD+AI 2024, PRISMA 2020, ARRIVE 2.0, TREND 2004. Lengths and turnarounds are our own working figures, not standards. "}<b>{"Your target journal overrides everything here"}</b>{" — word limits, structure, abstract headings and reference styles are set by the journal and vary widely."}</p></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d1"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "26px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"The mistake this is built to catch"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"A clinician has treated fourteen patients with an uncommon condition over six years and writes them up as a case series. It is publishable, it will probably be accepted somewhere, and it throws away the most valuable thing in the folder. Because those fourteen came from a defined population over a defined period, there is a denominator — and a denominator turns a description into a rate with a confidence interval around it. That is a different claim, it falls under STROBE rather than under CARE, it is considered by a substantially wider set of journals, and it takes roughly one extra week to write. The work is identical up to the point where somebody asks how many patients passed through the service in the same period, which is a question a case series never asks. Nobody makes this mistake out of ignorance of statistics. They make it because the article type was decided in the first ten minutes and never revisited."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Authorship, plainly"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"If we write it, whose paper is it?"}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Yours. But that answer is only worth anything if the arrangement is the one the ICMJE actually describes, so here is the arrangement rather than a reassurance."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"prose rv rv-d1"} style={{ maxWidth: "none" }}> <p><b>{"The ICMJE sets four authorship criteria, and all four must be met."}</b>{" Substantial contributions to the conception or design of the work, or to the acquisition, analysis or interpretation of data; drafting the work or reviewing it critically for important intellectual content; final approval of the version to be published; and agreement to be accountable for all aspects of the work. The criteria are about contribution, not about job title."}</p> <p><b>{"Writing assistance, on its own, does not meet them."}</b>{" The ICMJE lists writing assistance, technical editing, language editing and proofreading among the activities that alone do not qualify a contributor for authorship, and says such contributors should be acknowledged with their specific contribution described. It further advises editors to require that the corresponding author obtain written permission from everybody acknowledged — so we supply that permission rather than leaving you to ask for it. Separately, the ICMJE requires disclosure of any sponsor’s role in the writing of the report, which is why the acknowledgement names who funded the assistance."}</p> <p><b>{"So the standing arrangement is this."}</b>{" A Pubrica writer is acknowledged, not authored. You conceive the work, you supply the clinical judgement and the interpretation, you approve the final version and you are accountable for it. We supply the acknowledgement wording and the written permission to use it, and we will not draft a manuscript for somebody who has not read it. Where a Pubrica contributor genuinely does meet all four criteria — which happens, most often on the analysis — we say so and let you decide what to do about it. Nothing in the ICMJE bars a writer from being an author; it is the contribution that decides, not the invoice."}</p> <p><b>{"That is the opposite of ghostwriting rather than a polite version of it."}</b>{" Ghostwriting is undisclosed authorship: a paper written by somebody whose involvement nobody is told about. Disclosed assistance is a named contribution in the acknowledgements with the funding stated. The difference is the disclosure, and it costs one sentence."}</p> <p><b>{"The same principle governs AI."}</b>{" Under the ICMJE Recommendations as updated in January 2026, a chatbot cannot be listed as an author, because it cannot be accountable. AI used for writing assistance is declared in the acknowledgements. AI used for data collection, analysis or figure generation is described in the methods in enough detail to replicate the approach, including the tool, the version and the prompts. Authors remain responsible for checking output that can be authoritative-sounding and wrong, and AI-generated material cannot be cited as a primary source. We declare to you anything we use, and we follow whatever your target journal requires on top."}</p> </div> <div className={"caps__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ border: "1px solid var(--rule)", marginTop: "24px" }}> <p className={"caps__k"}>{"Settle the author list before the first draft, not after it"}</p> <p className={"caps__t"}>{"Almost every authorship dispute we have seen arrived the same way: nobody wrote it down. The registrar who collected the data assumed they were second; the consultant who suggested the question assumed they were last; the statistician was not asked. By the time it surfaces there is a manuscript, a submission deadline and a grievance, and the conversation that would have taken ten minutes in month one takes a department head in month nine. We ask for the author list and the order in writing at the first meeting, checked against the four criteria and revisited if contributions change. It is the least popular thing we ask for and the one that has saved the most trouble."}</p> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-our-experts-1x3gnad"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Our experts"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The people who will actually do the work."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Not a pool you are allocated from. The same named team stays with your project from scoping to delivery, the handover says which of them did which stage, and your project coordinator introduces them by name before anything starts."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"revw"}> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"SME"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Subject expert"}</b><span>{"A subject matter expert assigned from your topic, not from a rota"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Decides what the work is allowed to claim. Matched to your topic rather than allocated from a rota, and the one who tells you plainly when the evidence will not carry the conclusion you were hoping for."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Question, scope, interpretation"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"ICMJE, COPE, PRISMA"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Field"}</span><b>{"Matched to your topic"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DD"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Divya"}</b><span>{"PhD in Life Science · second reviewer"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Reads independently of the first pass and reconciles, because most errors in this work are transcription errors rather than reasoning ones. Disagreements are logged and adjudicated, never quietly resolved."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Independent second read"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"RoB 2, ROBINS-I, QUADAS-3, JBI"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Adjudicated by"}</span><b>{"A third reviewer"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"MJ"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Mr. John"}</b><span>{"M.Sc. in Statistics · statistician"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Owns anything the numbers decide. Says before the analysis exists whether the data can answer the question, and hands over the code so the whole thing can be re-run without us."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Analysis and certainty"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"GRADE, SWiM, CONSORT"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Tools"}</span><b>{"R, Stata, SAS, RevMan"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"revw__c rv"}> <div className={"revw__top"}>  <span className={"revw__ph"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span>{"DA"}</span></span> <span className={"revw__nm"}><b>{"Dr. Antony"}</b><span>{"Information specialist"}</span></span> </div> <div className={"revw__body"}> <p className={"revw__d"}>{"Finds what the work is built on. Writes the search line by line for each platform and hands it over dated and reproducible, so a reviewer, an editor or an assessor can run it again."}</p> <div className={"revw__st"}> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Owns"}</span><b>{"Search and retrieval"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Reads against"}</span><b>{"PRISMA-S, PRESS"}</b></div> <div className={"revw__r"}><span>{"Second-checked by"}</span><b>{"A second information specialist"}</b></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-sample-work-1lmeyi9"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Sample work"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"The scoping note that arrives first."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Before a quote and long before a draft, you get a written answer to four questions: what the data makes, who the authors are, what the paper may claim, and which journals will consider it. This is a real scoping note with the identifying detail changed. Use the tabs, then open the full note below to read it on this page."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"sample"}> <div className={"doc rv"}> <p className={"doc__k"}>{"Manuscript scoping note"}</p> <h3 className={"doc__h"}>{"14 patients, six years, one service · series or cohort?"}</h3> <p className={"doc__sub"}>{"The article type · the author list · the claim audit · the journal band"}</p> <div className={"doc__tabs"} role={"tablist"} aria-label={"Parts of the scoping note"}> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"pm-t1"} aria-controls={"pm-p1"} aria-selected={"true"} tabIndex={0}><i>{"1"}</i>{"Article type"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"pm-t2"} aria-controls={"pm-p2"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"2"}</i>{"Authorship"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"pm-t3"} aria-controls={"pm-p3"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"3"}</i>{"Claim audit"}</button> <button type={"button"} className={"doc__tab"} role={"tab"} id={"pm-t4"} aria-controls={"pm-p4"} aria-selected={"false"} tabIndex={-1}><i>{"4"}</i>{"Journal band"}</button> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"pm-p1"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"pm-t1"}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"?"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"What the author asked for"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"“A case series of our fourteen patients with this condition, for a specialty journal.” A reasonable request, and the first thing we questioned."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"The question nobody had asked"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"How many patients passed through the service in the same six years? Answer: 2,310. That figure turns fourteen descriptions into an incidence with a confidence interval, which is a different claim entirely."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Recommended type: retrospective cohort"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"With the series retained as a descriptive table inside it. Nothing is lost and a denominator is gained."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"Guideline: STROBE rather than CARE"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Which changes the structure, so it had to be settled before drafting rather than after. A paper restructured afterwards reads like one."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"What it costs to do it this way"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"About one extra week, and a records search to confirm the denominator. What it buys is a wider set of journals and a paper that will still be cited in five years."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"One question changed the article type"}</span><span>{"Asked in week one, not at review"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"pm-p2"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"pm-t2"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Criterion 1 · substantial contribution"}</dt><dd>{"To conception or design, "}<i>{"or"}</i>{" to acquisition, analysis or interpretation of data. Four of the six people proposed met this. The registrar who extracted every record met it clearly and had been left off."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Criterion 2 · drafting or critical revision"}</dt><dd>{"For important intellectual content. Reading a draft and saying “fine by me” does not meet it, and one proposed author was in that position."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Criterion 3 · final approval"}</dt><dd>{"Of the version to be published. Straightforward, and the one everybody remembers."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Criterion 4 · accountability"}</dt><dd>{"Agreement to be accountable for all aspects of the work, including investigating questions about accuracy or integrity. This is the criterion that makes honorary authorship a problem rather than a courtesy."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Outcome"}</dt><dd>{"Five authors, one moved to the acknowledgements with their contribution described and their written permission obtained, and one added who had not been on the list."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"The Pubrica writer"}</dt><dd>{"Acknowledged, not authored, with the wording supplied and written permission given: writing assistance does not on its own meet the criteria, and the ICMJE says it should be acknowledged."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Agreed in writing"}</dt><dd>{"In week one. Ten minutes then; a departmental conversation if it waits until month nine."}</dd></dl> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"pm-p3"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"pm-t3"} hidden={true}> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“Our protocol reduced complications from 19% to 7%”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Two problems. “Reduced” is causal and this is a before-and-after comparison in one service with no control. And the two periods differ in more than the protocol — case mix, staffing and referral pattern all changed. Rewritten to report both rates with intervals and to name the secular trend explicitly."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“This is the largest series reported to date”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Checkable, and it was not. Two larger series exist, one in a non-English journal. Rewritten to describe the series accurately, which is a better sentence anyway because it does not invite a reviewer to go and look."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“Should be adopted as standard practice”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"A practice recommendation from an uncontrolled single-centre series of fourteen. Rewritten to say the findings support a prospective evaluation. This is the sentence authors resist most and the one that changes how everything before it is read."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"!"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“No patients were lost to follow-up”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"True of the fourteen included, but three eligible patients were excluded because their records were incomplete — which is loss by another name. Rewritten with a flow figure showing every exclusion and its reason."}</span></span></div> <div className={"dex"}><span className={"dex__n"}>{"✓"}</span><span className={"dex__j"}>{"“Median follow-up 41 months”"}<span className={"dex__r"}>{"Kept. Accurate, checkable, and the strongest sentence in the draft."}</span></span></div> <p className={"doc__foot"} style={{ border: "0" }}><span>{"4 of 5 claims rewritten"}</span><span>{"None of them because the work was weak"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"doc__pane"} id={"pm-p4"} role={"tabpanel"} aria-labelledby={"pm-t4"} hidden={true}> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"As a case series"}</dt><dd>{"Specialty case report journals and the case sections of two society journals. Publishable, modest reach, rarely cited beyond the specialty."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"As a retrospective cohort"}</dt><dd>{"The same specialty journals plus their main research sections, and two general clinical titles that do not consider case series at all."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Realistic first choice"}</dt><dd>{"Named, with the reasoning: this journal has published three comparable single-centre cohorts in the past two years, so the design and the scale are within what it takes."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"Two fallbacks"}</dt><dd>{"Named in order, with what each charges, and with a note on which of the three has the shortest published time to first decision."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What will be challenged"}</dt><dd>{"The single centre, the before-and-after comparison, and the absence of a control period. All three answered in the discussion in advance rather than left for the response letter."}</dd></dl> <dl className={"dnt"}><dt>{"What we advised against"}</dt><dd>{"A journal that had emailed the author directly offering rapid publication. We explain why when we decline to submit somewhere, rather than simply not mentioning it."}</dd></dl> </div> <p className={"doc__foot"}><span>{"Redacted extract · author and study details changed"}</span><span>{"Delivered before the quote"}</span></p> </div> <div className={"rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"prose"}> <p>{"The scoping note is the deliverable that arrives before you have paid for anything. "}<b>{"Use the tabs to see each part."}</b></p> <p><b>{"The first tab is the one that matters."}</b>{" One question — how many patients passed through the service in the same period — moved this paper from a case series to a retrospective cohort. Nobody had asked it, because the article type had been decided in the first conversation and never revisited."}</p> <p><b>{"The authorship tab is the one people find uncomfortable."}</b>{" It moved somebody off the author list and added somebody who had been left off. Both changes were correct, both were awkward, and both were far easier in week one than they would have been after submission."}</p> </div> <div className={"factors"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Article type settled before drafting"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Because it decides the structure, not the wording."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Author list checked against all four criteria"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"In writing, in week one, and revisited if contributions change."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Every claim checked against the design"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"With the rewrite supplied, not just the objection."}</span></span></div> <div className={"factors__row"}><i /><span><b>{"Journals argued from what they publish"}</b><span className={"factors__d"}>{"Not from impact factor, and not from a solicitation email."}</span></span></div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note"} style={{ marginTop: "26px" }}>{"Ask for the sample work and you get a scoping note built round a study like yours — same design, same specialty, same target journals."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions"} style={{ marginTop: "16px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"#fsm-pm"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pm"}>{"Read the full scoping note"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/insights/sample-work/"}>{"Discover more"}</a> </div> </div> </div> <div className={"fsm rv rv-d2"} data-fsm={""}> <button type={"button"} className={"fsm__t"} data-fsm-t={""} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"fsm-pm"}> <span><b>{"Read the full scoping note"}</b><em>{"The whole deliverable, on this page — the article type, the authorship assessment, the claim audit, the journal band and the plan"}</em></span> <i aria-hidden={"true"} /> </button> <div className={"fsm__p"} id={"fsm-pm"}> <div className={"fsm__doc"}> <p className={"fsm__k"}>{"Physician manuscripts · sample scoping note"}</p> <h3 className={"fsm__hd"}>{"Manuscript scoping note — single-service experience, six years"}</h3> <p className={"fsm__sub"}>{"A real scoping note with the specialty, the condition, the institution and every identifying detail changed. Delivered before the quote, at no cost. Ask us and we will send one built around a study like yours."}</p> <h4><span>{"1"}</span>{"What you sent, and what you asked for"}</h4> <p>{"Fourteen patient records from one service over six years, a partial draft of about 1,400 words written as a case series, and a target journal in your specialty. The request was to write it up as a case series and submit."}</p> <p>{"The draft is clinically sound and the records are unusually complete. The recommendation below is not about the quality of the work. It is about the article type, which was settled early and, in our reading, settled wrongly."}</p> <h4><span>{"2"}</span>{"What the data makes"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Question"}</th><th>{"Answer"}</th><th>{"What it changes"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Were the fourteen consecutive?"}</td><td>{"Yes — every patient meeting the criteria in the period."}</td><td>{"A consecutive series is a stronger claim than a selected one, and it needs saying explicitly."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Is there a denominator?"}</td><td>{"Yes. 2,310 patients passed through the service in the same six years."}</td><td>{"This is the decisive fact. It converts fourteen descriptions into an incidence with a confidence interval."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Is the comparison period usable?"}</td><td>{"Partly. The six years before the protocol change are retrievable but the coding changed in year two."}</td><td>{"Usable with the change described. Not usable if the change is left unmentioned."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Recommended article type"}</td><td>{"Retrospective cohort study, with the fourteen retained as a descriptive table."}</td><td>{"Nothing is lost and a rate is gained."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Reporting guideline"}</td><td>{"STROBE (2007), with RECORD if the denominator comes from routinely collected data."}</td><td>{"A different structure from CARE, which is why it is settled now rather than at drafting."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Extra work"}</td><td>{"Approximately one week, plus a records search to confirm the denominator."}</td><td>{"The only cost of doing it the better way."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"3"}</span>{"Authorship, assessed against the four ICMJE criteria"}</h4> <p>{"Six people were proposed. The assessment below is ours and is advisory; the decision is the corresponding author’s, and the criteria are the ICMJE’s."}</p> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Contributor"}</th><th>{"Contribution as described"}</th><th>{"Assessment"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"Consultant A"}</td><td>{"Conceived the question, treated eleven of the patients, revised the draft, approves it, accountable."}</td><td>{"Meets all four. Corresponding author."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Consultant B"}</td><td>{"Treated three patients, contributed to interpretation, revised critically."}</td><td>{"Meets all four."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Registrar C"}</td><td>{"Extracted every record, built the dataset, drafted the results."}</td><td>{"Meets all four — and was not on the proposed list. Added."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Statistician D"}</td><td>{"Will design and run the analysis and interpret it, will revise the statistical sections."}</td><td>{"Meets all four once the work is done. Named now, confirmed at submission."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Consultant E"}</td><td>{"Read the draft and agreed with it."}</td><td>{"Does not meet criterion 2. Moved to acknowledgements with the contribution described and written permission obtained. This was the awkward one."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Head of department F"}</td><td>{"Named as a courtesy; no stated contribution."}</td><td>{"Does not meet any criterion. Honorary authorship, and criterion 4 is the reason it matters: an author agrees to be accountable for the whole paper."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Pubrica writer"}</td><td>{"Writing assistance and drafting under the authors’ direction."}</td><td>{"Acknowledged, not authored. Writing assistance does not by itself qualify; the acknowledgement wording and written permission are supplied by us."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"Two changes, both uncomfortable, both far cheaper in week one than after submission. We put this in writing at the start on every project for exactly this reason."}</p> <h4><span>{"4"}</span>{"Claim audit on the existing draft"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"As written"}</th><th>{"Problem"}</th><th>{"Rewritten as"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"“Our protocol reduced complications from 19% to 7%”"}</td><td>{"Causal verb for an uncontrolled before-and-after comparison, in a period when case mix and staffing also changed."}</td><td>{"Both rates reported with confidence intervals, the secular change named, and the comparison described as uncontrolled."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“The largest series reported to date”"}</td><td>{"Checkable and untrue. Two larger series exist, one in a non-English journal."}</td><td>{"The series described accurately, without the superlative. A better sentence, because it does not invite a reviewer to go and check."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“Should be adopted as standard practice”"}</td><td>{"A practice recommendation from fourteen uncontrolled patients in one centre."}</td><td>{"“These findings support prospective evaluation of the protocol in a multi-centre setting.”"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“No patients were lost to follow-up”"}</td><td>{"True of those included, but three eligible patients were excluded for incomplete records."}</td><td>{"A flow figure showing every exclusion with its reason, and the sentence removed."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"“Median follow-up 41 months”"}</td><td>{"None."}</td><td>{"Kept. The strongest sentence in the draft."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"5"}</span>{"Journal band"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Route"}</th><th>{"What opens up"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"As a case series"}</td><td>{"Specialty case report journals and two society case sections. Publishable; limited reach."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"As a retrospective cohort"}</td><td>{"The same journals’ main research sections, plus two general clinical titles that do not consider case series at all."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"First choice"}</td><td>{"Named in the full note, with the reasoning: three comparable single-centre cohorts published there in the past two years, so design and scale are within range."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Fallbacks"}</td><td>{"Two, in order, with charges and published time to first decision for each."}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"Advised against"}</td><td>{"A journal that emailed the corresponding author offering rapid publication for a fee. We say why rather than simply leaving it off the list."}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <h4><span>{"6"}</span>{"What we would do, and in what order"}</h4> <div className={"fsm__wrap"}><table> <thead><tr><th>{"Stage"}</th><th>{"Work"}</th><th>{"Working days"}</th></tr></thead> <tbody> <tr><td>{"1"}</td><td>{"Confirm the denominator from service records; agree author list in writing."}</td><td>{"3"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"2"}</td><td>{"Framework to STROBE, with words allocated and every section mapped to its checklist item."}</td><td>{"2"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"3"}</td><td>{"Analysis: incidence with intervals, the before-and-after comparison with its limitations modelled, descriptive table of the fourteen."}</td><td>{"4"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"4"}</td><td>{"Full draft, tables and the flow figure."}</td><td>{"6"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"5"}</td><td>{"Internal review by a second reader, claim audit repeated, STROBE checklist completed with page numbers, originality and AI screening."}</td><td>{"2"}</td></tr> <tr><td>{"6"}</td><td>{"Formatting, declarations, cover letter, submission."}</td><td>{"1"}</td></tr> </tbody> </table></div> <p className={"fsm__nt"}>{"What this note does not do is promise acceptance. It tells you what the data supports, what the paper may claim, and which journals publish work of this design and size. The decision belongs to an editor, and anybody telling you otherwise is describing something they do not control."}</p> <div className={"fsm__foot"}> <p>{"Prepared by Pubrica. Pubrica is a trading name of Guires"}<sup className={"reg"}>{"®"}</sup>{", registered in England, Wales and India."}</p> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/downloads/pubrica-physician-manuscript-sample.pdf"} download={""}>{"Download this as a PDF"}</a> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"What a Pubrica manuscript delivers"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What it gives you."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A paper written as the thing it actually is, claiming what its design can carry, with the authorship settled before anybody is upset about it."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"bens rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"01"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"The right article type, decided from the data"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Not from what the last paper was. It decides the reporting guideline, the structure, the journals that will consider the work and what the paper may claim — and it is settled in week one, in writing, when changing it still costs a week rather than a rewrite."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"02"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Claims proportionate to the design"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"Association described as association. A null result reported with its interval rather than as an absence of difference. Subgroups with their interaction tests. Over-reading your own data is the fastest way to have sound work returned, and it is entirely fixable in the words."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"03"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Authorship that will survive scrutiny"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"The list checked against all four ICMJE criteria and agreed in writing at the start, our contribution acknowledged rather than hidden, and the written permission for that acknowledgement supplied. The ten minutes nobody wants to spend in week one."}</span></span></div> <div className={"ben"}><span className={"ben__n"}>{"04"}</span><span><b className={"ben__b"}>{"Your clinical time back"}</b><span className={"ben__t"}>{"A full clinical manuscript takes a practising doctor somewhere between forty and eighty hours, spread across months of interrupted evenings, and published estimates in the medical writing field put it at forty to fifty hours for a professional. The parts only you can do — the question, the clinical judgement, the interpretation — are a small fraction of that."}</span></span></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-packages-e1hdf4"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Packages"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three tiers, with the scope printed beside the price."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Priced on article type, design, discipline, word count and target journal. Every figure is a floor with its cap beside it, because “from” on its own tells you nothing about what arrives."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"tiers rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Basic"}</span> <h3>{"Written to its guideline"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Early-career physicians and postgraduates preparing a first submission, or converting thesis data into a paper"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $320"}</b><span>{"up to 3,000 words · 1 target journal · 15 references"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"7–10 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The article type and reporting guideline settled in writing first"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The manuscript structured in IMRaD or your journal’s own structure"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Referencing in Vancouver, AMA or APA to the journal’s style"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Originality screening, with every match classified"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Formatting to one target journal, and one revision round"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: statistics; figures; journal selection; submission."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-pm"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pm"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Basic"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier tier--pick"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Advanced"}</span> <h3>{"With the analysis and the claim audit"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Practising physicians submitting original clinical research to Scopus- and PubMed-indexed journals"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $580"}</b><span>{"up to 4,500 words · 25 references · 4 tables or figures"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"10–15 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Basic"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Statistical analysis in R, SPSS, STATA or SAS, with the code returned"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The claim audit: every claim checked against the design, with rewrites supplied"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Literature synthesis establishing the gap rather than asserting it"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"The completed reporting checklist with page numbers"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Cover letter, declarations, and two revision rounds"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Internal review by a second reader who did not write it"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Add later: submission; graphical abstract; response to reviewers."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-pm"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pm"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Advanced"}</a> </div> <div className={"tier"}> <span className={"tier__k"}>{"Premium"}</span> <h3>{"Handled through to a decision"}</h3> <p className={"tier__for"}>{"Senior consultants, hospital research teams and faculty with complex datasets and indexed targets"}</p> <p className={"tier__price"}><b>{"From $940"}</b><span>{"up to 6,000 words · 40 references · 8 tables or figures"}</span></p> <p className={"tier__turn"}>{"Delivery "}<b>{"15–20 business days"}</b></p> <ul> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Everything in Advanced"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Journal shortlist of three, argued from what each has recently published"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Submission through the portal, with conflict-screened reviewer suggestions"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"One round of point-by-point response to reviewers"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Reformatting for a second journal if the first declines"}</span></li> <li><i>{"✓"}</i><span>{"Medical illustration, surgical flowcharts or a graphical abstract"}</span></li> </ul> <p className={"tier__add"}>{"Further review rounds and a third journal are quoted separately."}</p> <a className={"tier__sample"} href={"#fsm-pm"} data-fsm-open={"fsm-pm"}>{"View a sample"}</a> <a className={"tier__order"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Select Premium"}</a> </div> </div> <p className={"jcard__note rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "22px" }}>{"Additions are quoted alongside any tier: statistical revalidation of an analysis somebody else ran; conversion of a thesis chapter into an article, which is a rewrite rather than a trim; reference reformatting compatible with Zotero, EndNote and Mendeley; native-speaker proofreading by an editor with a doctorate in the field; ethics and registration documentation; a CME or conference slide deck built from the same work; translation; resubmission formatting for a journal in a different field; and expedited delivery where capacity allows, quoted on capacity rather than on urgency. Article processing charges are paid by you directly to the journal and never passed through us."}</p> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d2"} style={{ marginTop: "24px" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/pricing/"} data-nav={""}>{"All pricing"}</a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-guarantee-1b76uud"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Guaranteed quality"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What we promise, and what we will not."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A manuscript can be excellent and still be rejected, because the decision belongs to an editor. Here are the terms before you commit to anything."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"gtee rv"}> <div className={"gtee__top"}> <p className={"gtee__k"}>{"The Pubrica guarantee"}</p> <h3 className={"gtee__h"}>{"We keep working until it is right."}</h3> <p className={"gtee__p"}>{"Revision until the manuscript meets the brief and the guideline it is written to, with no cap on rounds inside the scope agreed and support running for a full year from delivery. A refund does not get your paper published; it leaves you with the same data and less time."}</p> </div> <div className={"gtee__grid"}> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"01"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"365 days of revision support"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"On every tier, including Basic. Journals take months to answer and reviewers ask for things nobody anticipated, so support that expires in thirty days expires exactly when you need it."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"02"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Our error, our cost"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"A checklist item missed, a reference wrong, a formatting rule misread — if it came from us, correcting it is free and you hear about it from us first."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"03"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Delivered on the date agreed"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"Grant deadlines and thesis submission dates do not move. If a date is genuinely at risk you hear it early with what can be done, not on the day."}</p></div> <div className={"gtee__i"}><p className={"gtee__n"}>{"04"}</p><p className={"gtee__t"}>{"Your paper stays yours"}</p><p className={"gtee__d"}>{"We draft, argue a view and tell you plainly when we disagree with a claim. What goes in your name is settled by you, every time."}</p></div> </div> <p className={"gtee__foot"}><b>{"The limits, stated plainly."}</b>{" We cannot guarantee acceptance, and we will not promise publication in high-impact journals — that is an outcome nobody selling writing controls, and a supplier who promises it is describing somebody else’s decision. We do not offer revisions “until acceptance”, because tying a fixed fee to a journal’s decision is an open-ended promise dressed as a generous one; what we offer instead is a full year of uncapped revision inside the agreed scope, which is a commitment we can actually keep. We will not write a claim the design does not support, however it is framed. We do not fabricate, adjust or selectively report data, and we do not remove an inconvenient finding. We will not add an honorary author to a list, and we will say so when we are asked. We will not submit to a journal that solicited you by email with a promise of rapid publication, and we will tell you why. And where the honest answer is that the dataset makes a stronger short report than a weak full paper, that is what you will hear."}</p> </div> <div style={{ height: "clamp(26px,3vw,38px)" }} /> <div className={"pledges rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"A scoping note before you pay anything"}</p> <p>{"Somebody qualified in your field reads what you have and writes you the article type, the reporting guideline, the realistic journal band and an honest read of what the data can claim. Two business days, at no cost, with no obligation. That note occasionally says the work needs another analysis before it is writable — unwelcome in week one, and considerably better than at review."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Authorship settled at the start"}</p> <p>{"Who the authors are and in what order, agreed in writing at the first meeting against the four ICMJE criteria, and revisited if contributions change. Almost every authorship dispute we see arrived because nobody wrote it down, and by the time it surfaces there is a manuscript and a grievance rather than a conversation."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"GDPR, patient data and confidentiality"}</p> <p>{"A non-disclosure agreement is signed before any material moves, and writers and project staff are bound by internal confidentiality agreements as well. Unpublished data is held under the UK GDPR on access-controlled systems within a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, kept only as long as the project needs it, never used to train anything and never shared outside your project team. Where a dataset contains patient identifiers we ask you to remove them before sending rather than removing them ourselves, because de-identification is a decision your ethics approval governs."}</p> </div> <div className={"plg"}> <p className={"plg__h"}><i><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M5 12.6l4.4 4.4L19 7"} /></svg></i>{"Declared, not ghosted"}</p> <p>{"The ICMJE lists writing assistance among the activities that do not on their own qualify somebody for authorship, says such contributors should be acknowledged with their contribution described, and advises editors to require the corresponding author to obtain written permission from everybody acknowledged. So a Pubrica writer is named in the acknowledgements, we supply both the wording and the permission, and you keep authorship. Where a contribution does meet all four criteria we say so and let you decide. Any use of AI is declared to you and handled to the ICMJE’s January 2026 guidance."}</p> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-client-stories-1q3pnx0"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"In their words"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Three manuscripts, and what changed."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Rephrased from client feedback. Each quote is a placeholder until the named clinician has confirmed it in writing."}</p> </div> </div>  <div className={"tcar rv"}> <div className={"tcar__track"} data-tcar={""} tabIndex={0} role={"group"} aria-label={"Client testimonials, scrollable"}> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“They asked how many patients went through the service in the same period. Nobody had asked. It turned our series into a cohort study.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--c"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"CLINICAL"}<br />{"MEDICINE"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Retrospective"}<br />{"Cohort"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Consultant physician · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“The authorship conversation in week one was awkward and it saved us a departmental argument in month nine.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--b"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"SURGICAL"}<br />{"RESEARCH"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Outcome"}<br />{"Study"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Surgical registrar · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> <figure className={"tq"}> <blockquote>{"“Four of our five headline sentences claimed more than the design could support. They rewrote each one and showed me why.”"}</blockquote> <span className={"tq__cov"} aria-hidden={"true"}><span className={"mcov"}> <span className={"mcov__b mcov__b--e"}> <span className={"mcov__k"}>{"PUBLIC"}<br />{"HEALTH"}</span> <span className={"mcov__n"}>{"Observational"}<br />{"Study"}</span> <span className={"mcov__r"} /> </span> </span></span> <figcaption className={"tq__who"}> <span className={"tq__nm"}><b>{"Name to be confirmed"}</b></span> <span className={"tq__role"}>{"— Academic clinician · region to be confirmed"}</span> <span className={"tq__pub"}><b>{"Published in"}</b><span>{"Journal name to be added"}</span><i>{"—"}</i></span> </figcaption> </figure> </div> <div className={"tcar__foot"}> <a className={"btn btn--ghost tcar__more"} href={"/testimonial/"}>{"Explore more client testimonials"}</a> <div className={"tcar__dots"} data-tdots={""}><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot is-on"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 1"} /><button type={"button"} className={"tcar__dot"} aria-label={"Go to testimonial group 2"} /></div> <div className={"tcar__btns"}> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tprev={""} aria-label={"Previous testimonial"} disabled={true}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> <button type={"button"} className={"tcar__btn"} data-tnext={""} aria-label={"More testimonials"}><svg viewBox={"0 0 24 24"} aria-hidden={"true"}><path d={"M9 5l7 7-7 7"} fill={"none"} stroke={"currentColor"} strokeWidth={"1.6"} strokeLinecap={"round"} strokeLinejoin={"round"} /></svg></button> </div> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""} id={"pn-physician-manuscripts-faq-qgx437"} data-pn={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"} style={{ display: "block" }}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Physician manuscript FAQs"}</p> <h2>{"Nine questions clinicians ask."}</h2> <p className={"prose"} style={{ marginTop: "20px" }}>{"Not sure what your data makes, or whether your author list would survive a journal asking? "}<a className={"tlink"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Ask an expert"}</a>{" — no quote required."}</p> </div> <div className={"faq__list rv rv-d1"}> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pm-0"}><span>{"What should be included in a physician-authored research manuscript?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pm-0"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Structurally: a title, a structured abstract to the journal’s own headings, keywords, then introduction, methods, results and discussion, with references, tables, figures and declarations around them. But the structure is the easy half. What decides whether the paper can be judged is the reporting guideline the design falls under, because that determines what each section is responsible for — CONSORT 2025 for a randomised trial, STROBE for cohort, case-control and cross-sectional studies, STARD for diagnostic accuracy, TRIPOD+AI for prediction models, PRISMA 2020 for systematic reviews, CARE for case reports, SQUIRE 2.0 for quality improvement. Take the current checklist from the EQUATOR Network, write to it from the outline stage rather than checking against it at the end, and complete it honestly. The gaps it exposes are exactly the ones a reviewer will find, and finding them yourself costs a paragraph where finding them at review costs three months."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pm-1"}><span>{"How do I know which type of manuscript my data makes?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pm-1"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Three questions settle it most of the time. Is there a denominator — a defined population the cases came out of? If yes, you have a rate rather than a description, and that is a study rather than a series. Did you do something to the patients, and if so was the allocation random? That separates a trial from an observational study and decides between CONSORT and STROBE. And are you comparing groups, or describing one? A comparison brings a whole additional set of reviewer questions about how the groups were formed and whether they were comparable. The router at the top of this page walks through those questions and a few more. The mistake we see most often is not a hard call between two types; it is a type that was decided in the first ten minutes and never revisited, usually because the last paper from the department was a series."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pm-2"}><span>{"What are the authorship criteria for physician research publications?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pm-2"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"The ICMJE sets four and all four must be met. Substantial contributions to the conception or design of the work, or to the acquisition, analysis or interpretation of data; drafting the work or reviewing it critically for important intellectual content; final approval of the version to be published; and agreement to be accountable for all aspects of the work, including investigating and resolving questions about its accuracy or integrity. Three practical consequences follow. Collecting data without contributing to design, analysis or interpretation does not by itself qualify somebody, though it very often should when you look at what they actually did. Reading a draft and approving it does not meet criterion two. And honorary authorship for a department head who contributed nothing fails criterion four in a way that matters: an author is agreeing to be accountable for the whole paper, which is not a courtesy to hand out. Writing assistance, technical editing, language editing and proofreading are listed by the ICMJE as activities that alone do not qualify a contributor, and such contributors should be acknowledged with their specific contribution described."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pm-3"}><span>{"If you write my paper, are you the author?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pm-3"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No. A Pubrica writer is acknowledged, not authored, and the acknowledgement is what makes the arrangement legitimate rather than what exposes it. Writing assistance does not on its own meet the ICMJE criteria; the ICMJE says such contributors should be acknowledged with their contribution described, and advises editors to require the corresponding author to obtain written permission from everybody acknowledged — so we supply that permission with the wording rather than leaving you to ask. The ICMJE also requires disclosure of any sponsor’s role in writing the report, which is why the acknowledgement names who paid for the assistance. Where a Pubrica contributor genuinely meets all four criteria — which happens most often on the statistical analysis — we say so and let you decide; nothing bars a writer from being an author, it is the contribution that decides. What we will not do is draft a manuscript for somebody who has not read it, because criterion four is a real undertaking."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pm-4"}><span>{"Can you turn my thesis chapter into a journal article?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pm-4"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Yes, and it is a rewrite rather than a trim, which is the part that surprises people. A thesis chapter is written to demonstrate competence to an examiner: the literature review is exhaustive because breadth is being assessed, the methods narrate what you learned as you went, and the discussion covers everything. A paper is written to convince a reviewer of one claim inside a word limit, so the literature review becomes two paragraphs that establish a gap, the methods become a reproducible account with the false starts removed, and the discussion argues a single point. It is also common that one chapter contains two papers, or that two chapters make one, and deciding that is the first conversation. Two practical points. Check your university’s policy on publishing from a deposited thesis, because some repositories make the chapter publicly available and a journal may treat that as prior publication. And settle authorship with your supervisor in writing before drafting rather than after. Note that this is different from writing a thesis for submission, which we do not do — see the question below."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pm-5"}><span>{"Will you write my thesis or dissertation for me?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pm-5"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No. We do not write theses, dissertations or any other assessed work to be submitted as a student’s own. In England, providing, arranging or advertising such a service is a criminal offence under sections 27 and 28 of the Skills and Post-16 Education Act 2022. In Australia, providing or advertising academic cheating services is an offence under the TEQSA Act as amended in 2020, carrying penalties of up to 500 penalty units and two years’ imprisonment. Universities’ academic integrity regulations prohibit a third party completing assessed work and typically permit only limited editing and proofreading within declared boundaries. What we do instead is work inside those boundaries: language editing and proofreading where your institution permits it and to the extent it permits, statistical analysis and its interpretation as a named collaborator, and conversion of an "}<i>{"already-examined"}</i>{" thesis chapter into a journal article, which is a publication rather than an assessment. If you are unsure where your institution draws the line, ask your supervisor or research office before you ask us — and we will ask you what the answer was."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pm-6"}><span>{"How can a research team standardise its manuscript workflow?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pm-6"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Five things, in order of how much trouble each one prevents. Decide the article type and the reporting guideline before drafting, and record both — this is the decision that costs a rewrite if it is wrong. Write the author list down at the start against the four ICMJE criteria, with a rule for what happens when contributions change. Agree a framework before prose, mapping every section to the checklist item it answers, so a section moving costs a minute rather than breaking every cross-reference. Have somebody who did not write the draft read it against the design, because authors cannot see their own claims. And keep one reference library per project rather than per author, because merging three libraries at submission is where the wrong-year citations come from. For departments producing several papers a year we set this up once as a written house workflow, with templates, and it is usually the cheapest thing we do."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pm-7"}><span>{"Do you guarantee publication in a high-impact journal?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pm-7"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"No, and neither can anybody else. Acceptance is an editor’s decision informed by reviewers, and a supplier who promises it is selling you something they do not control. We will also not offer “unlimited revisions until acceptance”, which is the same promise wearing a different coat: it ties a fixed fee to an outcome outside the contract, and it is unenforceable in the direction that matters to you. What we do instead is commit to what we can actually deliver — a full year of uncapped revision inside the agreed scope from the date of delivery, on every tier. Within that year a reviewer asking for a reanalysis, a journal changing its format or a co-author joining late are all included. New work is not: a different study, a second paper from the same dataset, or a rewrite for a journal in another field. We say which side of that line something falls on before starting rather than after."}</p></div></div></div> <div className={"faq__item"}><h3 className={"faq__h"}><button className={"faq__q"} aria-expanded={"false"} aria-controls={"pm-8"}><span>{"My paper was rejected. Is it worth revising or should I send it elsewhere?"}</span><span className={"sign"} aria-hidden={"true"} /></button></h3><div className={"faq__a"} id={"pm-8"} role={"region"}><div><p>{"Read the letter for which of three things it says, because they have different answers. A desk rejection on scope means the paper was never read: send it elsewhere, unchanged, and spend the time choosing better. A rejection with substantive reviewer comments is the most valuable document you will receive about this paper, and sending it elsewhere without addressing them is the commonest expensive mistake in publishing — specialty reviewer pools are small, and the same person may well read it again at the next journal. A rejection that questions the design or the analysis is the one to take seriously: sometimes there is a fix, sometimes the honest answer is a shorter paper making a smaller claim, and occasionally it is that the study cannot support a paper at all. We will read the letter with you and say which of the three it is, including when the answer is the one nobody wants."}</p></div></div></div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} style={{ background: "var(--paper-2)", borderBlock: "1px solid var(--rule)" }} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Related services"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"What sits either side of the manuscript."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"A paper needs a study behind it and an editor in front of it, and both are work in their own right."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"rel"}> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"1"}</span><b>{"IF IT IS A PARTICULAR KIND OF PAPER"}</b><em>{"the three with their own pages"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/case-report/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Case report writing"}</b><span>{"One patient, written to CARE, with the consent handled before drafting."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/physician-writing-services/original-research-article/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Original research article"}</b><span>{"A study with a denominator, written to the guideline its design requires."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"2"}</span><b>{"THE WORK BEHIND IT"}</b><em>{"evidence, design and numbers"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"#/clinical-literature-review"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Clinical literature review"}</b><span>{"What the literature actually says, synthesised and graded."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/research-services/biostatistics-and-statistical-programming-services/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Biostatistics and programming"}</b><span>{"The analysis behind the numbers, with assumptions checked rather than assumed."}</span></a> </div> <div className={"rel__col rv"}> <p className={"rel__stage"}><span className={"rel__n"}>{"3"}</span><b>{"GETTING IT ACCEPTED"}</b><em>{"the editor and the reviewer"}</em></p> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/journal-selection/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Journal selection"}</b><span>{"Which journals publish this design at this size, decided from the manuscript."}</span></a> <a className={"rel__item"} href={"/services/publication-support/peer-review-pre-submission/"} data-nav={""}><b>{"Pre-submission peer review"}</b><span>{"The objection heard before an editor’s reviewer makes it."}</span></a> </div> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap"}> <div className={"shead rv"}> <p className={"shead__tag"}>{"Insights"}</p> <div className={"shead__body"}> <h2>{"Further reading on manuscripts and journals."}</h2> <p className={"lede"}>{"Three pieces from our library on structure, journal choice and writing for readers outside the specialty."}</p> </div> </div> <div className={"reads rv rv-d1"}> <a className={"read"} href={"https://pubrica.com/academy/physician-writing/how-to-structure-case-reports-review-articles-journals/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How to structure case reports and review articles for medical journals"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Medical journals expect a set structure, with clear objectives and a reporting guideline behind each section."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-should-physicians-choose-the-right-journal-for-submitting-a-case-report/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How should physicians choose the right journal for submitting a case report?"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Publishing takes more than clinical knowledge; it demands a strategic read of which journals still publish what, and how."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> <a className={"read"} href={"/insights/how-physicians-can-write-clear-and-impactful-patient-education-materials/"}><span className={"read__k"}>{"Article"}</span><span><b className={"read__b"}>{"How physicians can write clear and impactful patient education materials"}</b><span className={"read__d"}>{"Patient education materials carry health literacy. Clear ones change adherence; unclear ones quietly cost it."}</span></span><span className={"read__go"} aria-hidden={"true"}>{"→"}</span></a> </div> </div> </section> <section className={"section section--tight section--dark"} data-rv-group={""}> <div className={"wrap cta cta__in"}> <div className={"rv"}> <h2>{"Send what you have. You get the scoping note before the quote."}</h2> <p className={"lede"} style={{ marginTop: "18px" }}>{"What the data makes, which guideline governs it, what the paper may claim and which journals publish work of this design and size — in two business days, at no cost and with no obligation."}</p> </div> <div className={"hero__actions rv rv-d1"} style={{ margin: "0" }}> <a className={"btn btn--primary"} href={"/order-now/"}>{"Get a free quote"}</a> <a className={"btn btn--ghost"} href={"/contact-us/"}>{"Contact us"}</a> </div> </div> </section> </main>
